# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-13: a full-screen page opened from a row of the listing goes back
# to the **listing**, not out to the adventuring screen (M5-E4d, #305) —
# and the second Escape is what gives the screen back.
#
# Two claims, and the leg is shaped around the difference between them.
# The first is that the frame after the page closes is the listing again:
# it cannot be `equal` to the listing *before* the page, because opening
# a row takes the `*` off it, so the row the cursor is on changes. So the
# listing after is held still instead, which says it is a settled screen
# and not a page with a listing painted through it.
#
# The second is `not-log-giveback.leg`'s, restated one level in: the
# adventuring screen before `Notes` is the adventuring screen after the
# listing closes, every pixel but the bar row.
about a page from the listing goes back to the listing, and then out
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
cite-all
both code-wheel
# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), and this run
# drives past the challenge, so it needs it. Pinned by digest because a
# document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25

# **A screen this seam draws is slow to appear, and the ranges below are
# spaced for it.** It is painted over successive arrivals, a few rows at
# a time, and the program's own drawing routines are what put each row
# on the glass. Measured by hand on the shorter boot (#305): a
# twenty-row page takes about 230 frames to settle after the key that
# opened it and a ten-row listing about 130. That is the listing's own
# behaviour since #222 rather than anything the page added; a `same`
# range that started sooner would be measuring the paint.

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
key N@10600
key Return@11200
key Escape@12200
key Escape@13200

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# The listing, the page, and the listing again: each settled.
same 10800-11175
same 11500-12175
same 12400-13175

equal 10600 13600 bar
